## 🔧 Quick Reference: Asset Usage Patterns

### Using Colors
```kotlin
// Resource reference
Text(
    text = "Hello",
    color = colorResource(R.color.primary)
)

// Compose Color direct
Text(
    text = "Hello",
    color = Colors.GreenPrimary
)
```

### Using Dimensions
```kotlin
// Padding
modifier = Modifier.padding(
    horizontal = dimensionResource(R.dimen.spacing_xl),
    vertical = dimensionResource(R.dimen.spacing_lg)
)

// Direct reference
modifier = Modifier.padding(
    horizontal = Spacing.xl,
    vertical = Spacing.lg
)
```

### Using Icons
```kotlin
// Vector Drawable (Scalable)
Icon(
    painter = painterResource(R.drawable.ic_upgrade),
    contentDescription = "Upgrade",
    modifier = Modifier.size(24.dp),
    tint = Color.Green
)

// PNG Image (Raster)
Image(
    painter = painterResource(R.drawable.stall_tea),
    contentDescription = "Tea Stall",
    modifier = Modifier.size(200.dp)
)
```

### Using Buttons
```kotlin
// Primary Button
PrimaryButton(
    text = "Upgrade",
    onClick = { viewModel.upgradeStall() }
)

// Tap Serve Button
TapServeButton(
    onClick = { viewModel.serveTap() },
    comboCount = gameState.comboCount
)
```

### Using Cards
```kotlin
// Info Card
InfoCard(
    title = "Stall Stats",
    subtitle = "Tea Stall Level 5"
) {
    Text("Income: ₹100/second")
}

// Character Card
CharacterCard(
    name = "Rajesh",
    level = 5,
    isPremium = false,
    onClick = { showCharacterDetails() }
)
```

### Using Progress
```kotlin
// Gate Progress
UnlockGateProgressBar(
    current = 4,
    total = 10,
    label = "Upgrades"
)

// Experience Bar
ExperienceBar(
    current = 250,
    total = 500
)

// Happiness Meter
HappinessMeter(
    happiness = 75
)
```

